═══ W-UPS-ONE-DOCACTION — E1 COMPILE: one DocAction executor per document (TEAMWORK_FRAMEWORK FL-7, §38.1) ═══
§U1 CONTROL
   🟢 P1 + the processor's order with ONE executor (HQ role 102, CO) compiles; no plan error — ok=true planErrors=[]
   🟢 the compiled plan CARRIES the executor on that row (what E2/E3 will read) — {"executor":102,"actions":["CO"]}
§U2 DUAL
   🟢 a second row giving C_Order another executor (the station) -> dual-docaction, the plan does not compile — [{"code":"dual-docaction","table":"c_order","rows":["D1 hq-order","D2 another-executor"]}]
§U3 STATION
   🟢 the station's UP declaration given a DocAction by its own role -> station-docaction — [{"code":"station-docaction","row":"F1 pos-sales-up"}]
§U4 AUTHOR
   🟢 executor "author" on a UP declaration -> docaction-author-not-mesh — [{"code":"docaction-author-not-mesh","row":"F1 pos-sales-up"}]
   🟢 executor "author" on a BOTH + space (peer team) row compiles — the device that authored the document is its one executor — []
§U5 BAD
   🟢 no executor -> docaction-bad — [{"code":"docaction-bad","row":"D1 hq-order"}]
   🟢 executor "x" -> docaction-bad — [{"code":"docaction-bad","row":"D1 hq-order"}]
   🟢 actions [] -> docaction-bad — [{"code":"docaction-bad","row":"D1 hq-order"}]
   🟢 actions ["ZZ"] -> docaction-bad — [{"code":"docaction-bad","row":"D1 hq-order"}]
§U6 GENERIC
   🟢 the same files with the document tables renamed (C_Order -> M_Movement, C_OrderLine -> M_MovementLine, C_Invoice -> M_Inventory) give the same verdicts: the rule knows no table — identical
